{
  "feature": "auth-processor",
  "kind": "online",
  "programs": [
    "COPAUA0C"
  ],
  "install": [
    "pending-authorizations"
  ],
  "notes": "Each case puts request messages on AWS.M2.CARDDEMO.PAUTH.REQUEST and runs trigger transaction CP00 once (MQTM via RETRIEVE). Pinned legacy defects: (1) WS-RESP-LENGTH (COPAUA0C line 46, VALUE 1) is the STRING POINTER in 6000-MAKE-DECISION (lines 722-730) and is never reset, and 7100-SEND-RESPONSE sends it as the length (line 756): every reply carries one extra trailing low-value byte, and each later reply in the same trigger repeats all earlier replies before its own. (2) 5000-PROCESS-AUTH (lines 438-468) does not reset WS-PAUT-SMRY-SEG-FLG, so a card-not-found request that follows a request with a summary is decided against the previous account's summary and approved with 00. WS-DECLINE-REASON-FLG is not reset either, but no reply can show it: every decline path that reaches the EVALUATE sets an earlier WHEN. Under the harness's fixed clock all detail keys of one trigger are equal, so a second request for the same account gets II on the detail ISRT; the cases use different accounts. Also pinned: 8400-UPDATE-SUMMARY copies ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT and ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT over the summary's limits on every write (lines 810-811), and a new summary is built with INITIALIZE ... REPLACING NUMERIC DATA BY ZERO (line 802), which leaves the alphanumeric status fields as they were in storage (low-values under the harness's -fdefaultbyte=0). Request fields an UNSTRING does not reach keep their storage contents too, which is why the malformed request's reply carries low-values.",
